data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (ships with .NET 11), the Cosmos DB provider **removes the sync-over-async opt-in entirely**. The `EnableSyncOverAsync()` configuration option is gone. All synchronous LINQ operators — `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`, etc. — now throw an **`InvalidOperationException`** unconditionally when used against the Cosmos provider.

## The fix

Convert to async equivalents:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- This only affects the **Cosmos DB provider** — the relational providers still support sync APIs.
- The change propagates up the call stack: controllers/services calling these methods must also become `async`.
- Remove any `EnableSyncOverAsync()` calls from your `DbContext` configuration — they'll produce a compile error.
